                # where the VM disagrees with itself (EigenScript#1074: the
                # write is invisible to the next body read yet persists
                # past the loop; a pre-bound local persists where a read-
                # only body loop-scopes, #1064). Read-only bodies are
                # coherent -- loop-scoped -- and emitted as such.
                local _lwr is collect_assigns of [fbody, {}]
                if _lwr[fvar] != null:
                    # (the name may be a `local`, a plain assign elsewhere in
                    # the function, or bound ONLY inside this loop -- the
                    # bound-set is whole-body containment and cannot tell
                    # those apart, so the message claims none of them: #195)
                    throw of ("AOT: '" + fvar + "' is a for binder over an INTERROGATED name that is not a parameter, and the loop body WRITES it. On the pinned VM that write is invisible to the next body read yet persists past the loop (EigenScript#1074; the #1064 family), so there is no one answer to emit; refused rather than picking one (ouroboros#187).")
                # (round 119) the round-116 refusal for a read-only body over
                # a local the function also binds outside the loop is LIFTED:
                # the per-call boundness bit (round 117) is exactly the
                # "did the other binding run first" fact it was waiting for.
                # t225 (pre-bound: 7 8 1 7), t226/t227 (binding after the
